  "summary": "pypdf: Possible long runtimes for repeated references to the same missing object",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes. This requires loading relevant parts of a file (like their pages) where the same, but non-existent indirect object is referenced multiple times.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.21.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.21.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4240](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4240).",
